# Temporary allowlist of known dbusage findings (I-G1). Protected tool area (D68).
# Format: <import|call> <repo-relative file> <reason>
# Findings in a listed file are printed as "expected" instead of failing the lint stage.
# Each unit that fixes a location removes its line; I-B15 empties the internal/store lines.
#
# internal/store: the package does not import dynamitedb at all yet (it bypasses the library with raw S3), so
# the rule has no import/call finding there; I-B15's new dynamitedb code is judged by the rule in full.
# No internal/store line is needed; if I-B15 adds one, it must remove it again.
#
# Found by I-G1 outside internal/store (owner: worker/logstore unit; remove when the worker stops importing lake):
import internal/worker/process.go internal/worker builds lake.NewString/NewInt rows directly; the lake schema belongs to internal/logstore
